-%-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
% readme_HMR_System_Tesc_Lc.txt
%-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
% In this directory we deal with NGRC DDE system learned from the HMR system;
%-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
% Here we list the files involved in this directory;
%-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
% HMR_scan_Lc_aut_vt2.m -> in this file the NGRC DDE system is learned by the
% HMR neurons model, and then the closed NGRC system is integrated independently,
% replicating the chaotic attractor; we here scan the NGRC parameter Lc, and for 
% each of them compute the statistics of escape time Tesc;
%-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
% HMR_signal.m -> this auxiliary function compues the dynamics of the original 
% HMR system with given initial conditions and for a given time interval with a 
% given time step; this function is used by the file [HMR_scan_Lc_aut_vt2.m];
%-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
% XPt_record.mat -> this data file contains the dynamics of closed NGRC DDE system, previously
% learned by the HMR neuron model; this dynamics is computed by program 
% [HMR_scan_Lc_aut_vt2.m] for specified value of Lc; the dynamics are plotted
% in the file [plot_XPt_v.m];
%-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
% plot_XPt_v.m -> this file plots the dynamics of NGRC DDE learned by HMR system;
% the data are taken from [XPt_record.mat];
%-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
% These files are auxiliary functions for the NGRC DDE system:
%----------------------------------------------------------------------------
% generate_all_exp_matreces.m
% generateCheb_feat_vect.m
% generateChebyshevs.m
% generateChebyshevsDiffLyap.m
% genExponents.m
%----------------------------------------------------------------------------
% matr.mat -> contains power matrices necessary for composing Tschebyshev
% polynomials;
